{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 (rebar-debug) — FIX LANDED FOR REVIEW (Gerrit change 2305).\n\n## Fix\nAdded pure helper `run_differs._scoped_selection_ids(selection_ids, typed_mutations)` that expands the shadow planner's selection ids to LOCAL IDS ∪ their BOUND JIRA KEYS, read purely from the mutations' own provenance (no binding_store I/O — the shadow layer stays side-effect-free). Wired it into the single `plan_pass` call site (run_differs.py). A bound-issue update (target=jira_key) is now recognized in-scope and planned `mutate`, so the live coordinator+fuse reroute executes the write — restoring parity with the legacy `_build_filter_target_set` path. Non-test diff: 35 lines in one file.\n\n## RED→GREEN (held out from the fix)\n- Held-out oracle `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_sync_only_scalar_update_dispatch_heldout.py` drives `reconcile_once` through a CLEAN subprocess (an in-memory transport records `update_issue`), avoiding the pytest conftest module-seeding collision. RED before the fix (`sync --only` dropped the write) / GREEN after; the `--filter-local-ids` parity guard stays GREEN throughout.\n- Mutation check (teeth): reverting the id-expansion returns the `--only` test to RED.\n- Refactoring litmus: the oracle asserts observable transport calls, not internals.\n- Pure-function teeth `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_scoped_selection_ids_af1b.py`: scoped expansion, unselected ticket NOT pulled in, create target unchanged.\n\n## Regression + gates\nFull reconciler unit suite `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` GREEN (3631 passed, 1 skipped). `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass. Plan-review (blast-escalated LLM tier) PASS + signed.\n\n## Sibling sweep (Step 7)\n- Axis 1 (construct): `plan_pass` has exactly ONE caller and there is exactly ONE `selection.ids` construction site — both the fixed site. `_scope_excluded` is only reached through that path. No other live instances.\n- Axis 2 (parity): all sync surfaces (CLI/MCP/library) funnel through `reconcile_once → run_differs → plan_pass`, so the fix at that shared core covers every channel. The legacy `--filter-local-ids` channel was already correct (guarded by the parity test). No MISSING slots.\n- Bonus: the same expansion corrects a latent `--except` case (an excepted bound ticket's jira-key-targeted update was not being excluded).\n\n## Fix-safety\nRestoration (restores parity with the legacy route), not creation. No new dependency. No pre-existing test weakened.\n\n## Attribution\nregression, caused_by 67d4-ecba-cf95-4353 (commit d49466b5). To be recorded on the bug close via `--caused-by`.\n\n## Remaining\nAwaiting Gerrit change 2305 gates (LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1). Live replication = the Jira DC External Integration lane, which must run GREEN before close."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787881914611778001,"uuid":"17b59d59-8fbe-498b-ab51-8660fb1bddb6"}